  "description": "Hand-seeded questions from real closed Illospace incidents and their resolving GitHub PRs. These are not claimed to be verbatim query-log entries. PHRASING RULE: every question describes only the OBSERVED SYMPTOM, in the words someone would use before they knew the cause. Internal vocabulary -- symbol names, file paths, subsystem nouns, and the rare phrases the ticket itself uses -- is banned, because a question carrying the document's own rare terms retrieves on lexical match and inflates recall. Every question here was rewritten under this rule after an adversarial review on 2026-08-03 graded the first draft 0 honest / 27 leaky / 2 wrong-evidence. Acceptable-evidence pointers are the items that actually ANSWER the question; an issue merely closed by the same PR is not automatically evidence.",
